{"name":"Marsh","hex":"#5c5337","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Marsh","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A topographic surname from Middle English for someone living by a marsh.","A number of places in England:\nA hamlet in Great and Little Kimble cum Marsh parish, Buckinghamshire, previously in Wycombe district .\nA small village in Yarcombe parish, East Devon district, Devon .\nA small suburb of Oxenhope, City of Bradford, West Yorkshire . \nA suburb of Cleckheaton, Kirklees borough, West Yorkshire . \nA western suburb of Huddersfield, Kirklees borough, West Yorkshire ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Marsh"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marsh","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a marsh is a wetland that is dominated by herbaceous plants rather than by woody plants. More in general, the word can be used for any low-lying and seasonally waterlogged terrain. In Europe and in agricultural literature, low-lying meadows that require draining and embanked polderlands are also referred to as marshes or marshland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg/330px-Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh","wikidata":"Q30198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marsh in shallow water on a lakeshore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoastal_marsh_profile.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White water lilies are a typical marsh plant in European areas of deeper water.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Many kinds of birds nest in marshes; this one is a yellow-headed blackbird.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AXanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Jyv%C3%A4skyl%C3%A4_-_swamp_2.jpg/500px-Jyv%C3%A4skyl%C3%A4_-_swamp_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Jyv%C3%A4skyl%C3%A4_-_swamp_2.jpg/1280px-Jyv%C3%A4skyl%C3%A4_-_swamp_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Jyv%C3%A4skyl%C3%A4_-_swamp_2.jpg/500px-Jyv%C3%A4skyl%C3%A4_-_swamp_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A marsh i